---
export const title = "Theme Selector";
export const jsFile = "themeSelector.js";
---

<h1>{title}</h1>

<div class="desc">
  This component is configured to detect the users current light/dark mode
  preferance and set its default state to match. It then allows users to change
  their theme with their choice saved to localStorage memory. Behind the scenes
  it simply toggles the "color-scheme" css value on :root to be either light or
  dark from its detault of "light dark".
  <br /><br />
</div>

<div class="demo-wrap">
  <rex-theme></rex-theme>
</div>
<h3>In Code</h3>
<div class="code-wrap">
  <pre><code class="usage language-javascript">
    {`
  // import the component
  import {rex-theme} from TBA;
  
  //use it in your HTML
  <rex-theme></rex-theme>
  `}
  </code></pre>
  <h3>In CSS</h3>
  <pre><code class="usage language-css css">
    {`
    /* make sure the color-scheme is set globally */
    :root {
        color-scheme: light dark;
    }

    /* define the variables */
    --accent: light-dark(#000, #fff);

    /* use the variables */
    h1{color:var(--accent)}
  `}
  </code></pre>
  <br />
  <section class="highlight">
    <h3>How it works</h3>
  </section>

  <script>
    import "../lib/themeSelector";
  </script>
</div>
